AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0009049> "An inflorescence is a reproductive shoot system from which at least two flowers develop. The growth pattern of an inflorescence may be monopodial (single main shoot axis), sympodial (growth only occurs from axillary meristems), or both. An inflorescence axis (PO:0020122) can be determinate or indeterminate. An inflorescence flower pedicel (PO:0009052) is the ultimate axis in an inflorescence. The flower (PO:0009046) of many plants, for example Magnolia spp., is solitary.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0009049> "inflorescence")
