AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0009059> "The corolla (PO:0009059) is part of the perianth (PO:0009058). This  definition is based on the complete flower, which has all four whorls. In many species, and in mutants one or more of the whorls may be missing. The corolla (PO:0009059) often functions to attract pollinators.")
